            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Today is **Monday, August 3, 2026** (US). Here are the most notable **Azure AI–related items reported today / very recently**:\n\n- **ArcelorMittal expands its partnership with Microsoft to accelerate AI-driven transformation on Azure** (customer/partner news). Multiple outlets report ArcelorMittal is deepening its use of **Microsoft Cloud/Azure** to strengthen data + AI capabilities and make Azure its primary cloud. ([thenextweb.com](https://thenextweb.com/news/arcelormittal-microsoft-azure-primary-cloud-ai))\n\n- **Microsoft’s latest official “what shipped” feeds are the best place to confirm Azure AI changes day-by-day**:\n  - **Azure Updates (official)**: Microsoft’s consolidated feed of platform updates. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n  - **Azure announcements blog page (official)**: Azure product announcements (not AI-only, but often includes AI platform items). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/content-type/announcements/))  \n\n- **Broader “Azure + AI demand” signal from Microsoft’s most recent earnings coverage** (not “today,” but recent and relevant): reporting highlights strong Azure momentum tied to AI infrastructure demand. ([finance.yahoo.com](https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/msft-q4-earnings-call-highlights-140000543.html))\n\nIf you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (e.g., **Azure AI Foundry/Foundry Models, Azure OpenAI, Azure AI Search, Fabric, Copilot Studio on Azure**), I can narrow this to the **specific sub-products** and list only the **AI-feature releases/GA/previews** from the official update feeds.",
